{
  "borough": "Enfield Council",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal has failed to demonstrate the development would not result in an increase in flood risk on or off site and suitable flood mitigation measures. The Flood Risk Assessment does not adequately demonstrate how it will not increase flood risk elsewhere throughout its lifetime for the 1 in 100 year plus climate change event, as no level for level flood compensation has been provided. The development therefore does not comply with Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010)  and Policies SI12 of the London Plan (2021), The Enfield Strategic Flood Risk Assessment (2021), Policies DMD59, DMD60, DMD61 and DMD62 of the Development Management Document (2014) and the NPPF (2024).\r\r",
    "The proposal has failed to demonstrate sufficient measures to promote Sustainable Drainage at the site and manage the risk of flooding. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021), CP21 of Core Strategy (2010) and DMD59, DMD60, DMD 61 and DMD62 of the Development Management Document (2014) and the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed dwelling does not reflect the architectural style of the Victorian terraces within which it would be immediately adjacent to. The proposed roof and fenestration pattern do not follow the prevailing styles of the existing Victorian terraces nor is the design of such a high quality that the dwelling would integrate and enhance the streetscene. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies D4 of the London Plan (2021), CP 30 of the Core Strategy (2010) and DMD8 and DMD 37 of the Development Management Document (2014) and the NPPF (2024)."
  ],
